// The application icon, for Explorer, Alt-Tab, and the settings window.
//
// Id 1 is deliberate: the shell shows the icon with the lowest numeric id, so a
// lower one added later would silently take over.
//
// NOTHING ELSE BELONGS IN THIS FILE. In particular, no manifest: build.rs
// embeds one through embed-manifest, and a second RT_MANIFEST resource produces
// an executable Windows refuses to start.
//
// assets/appicon.ico is generated by `cargo run -p altoggle-icongen`.
1 ICON "assets/appicon.ico"
